The class $\mathcal C$ is preserved by a channel step with $\lambda\in[0,1]$, by conditionally independent products of experiments, and by mixtures whose mixing label is observed and independent of the input. If $\mu,
u\in\mathcal C$ are the marginal posterior laws of two experiments, then their product posterior law $\mu\star
u$ satisfies  egin{align} \E_{\mu\star
u} A \leq{}& \E_{\mu}A+\E_{
u}A
otag\ &- rac{\E_{\mu}A^2\,\E_{
u}A+ \E_{\mu}A\,\E_{
u}A^2}{1000}. \end{align} In particular, when $\E_{\mu}A=\E_{
u}A=b$, the subtracted term is at least $2b^3/1000$.
